r long contexts and asks about KV cache offloading, prefix cache sharing, prompt caching for self-hosted models, LMCache with Valkey, or lower TTFT or GPU cost. Not for Bedrock prompt caching, LLM response or semantic caching, or general application caching.\n\nServices: elasticache, ec2\nTasks: deploy, optimize, troubleshoot\nPersona: developer, data-scientist, devops\nWorkload: ai-ml","skill_name":"caching-for-llm-inference"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"writing-agentcore-policy","skill_description":"Authors, validates and submits Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Policy statements (Cedar and Dogwood) for an AgentCore Gateway. Discovers the Gateway's targets and tools, generates the Gateway's Cedar schema, drafts permit/forbid, guardrail and temporal policies from access requirements or from a whole natural-language policy document (splitting it into rules, marking the rules that cannot be expressed, and repairing failing drafts in batches), checks them locally (syntax, schema, API limits, claim and guardrail pitfalls), and creates or updates them in a policy engine after explicit developer approval, reporting the final status and service findings. Use when a developer wants to write, translate, fix, validate or submit AgentCore Gateway policies, convert a policy document or a list of rules into policies, restrict which users or roles can call Gateway tools, add Bedrock guardrail or session-history (temporal) conditions, or resolve CreatePolicy/UpdatePolicy failures.\n\nServices: bedrock-agentcore-control, bedrock-agentcore\nTasks: design, deploy, debug, secure\nPersona: developer, security\nWorkload: agents, generative-ai","skill_name":"writing-agentcore-policy"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Find Claude Sonnet 5 global vs US per-token pricing"}
